---
title: Gaviidae
---
# Gaviidae

Gaviidae holds the loons, heavy-bodied northern waterbirds with a dagger bill
and a sharply patterned breeding plumage. They pursue prey from the surface
downward, driven by the feet, and routinely work at depths of several metres for
a minute or more. The eye focuses in air and in water alike through a
deformable lens, so a descending bird does not lose sight of its quarry. All
five species breed on northern lakes and winter at sea. See [[common-loon]].
